                <pb facs="0910" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg811"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1731/189: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-07T14:00:00-06:00">March 7, 1936—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 7—4:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>57. Department’s 29, March 6, 3 p.m. Information regarding Costa Rican and
                    Guatemalan negotiations apparently impressed favorably Nicaragua’s this morning.
                    Will telegraph further after afternoon session.</p>
                <p>Have decided to leave March 14 and have so advised Mr. Long who will presumably
                    arrive March 16.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
